---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Program = `let names          = ["Rivera", "Chen", "Okafor", "Sandoval"];
let priorSalary    = [52000, 41000, 55000, 38000];
let yearsExperience = [5, 5, 6, 6];

function offerFor(i)
{
  let offer = priorSalary[i] + (priorSalary[i] / 10);

  if (yearsExperience[i] >= 6)
  {
    offer = offer + 2000;
  }

  return offer;
}

for (let i = 0; i < names.length; i++)
{
  console.log(names[i] + ": " + offerFor(i));
}`;

const Output = `Rivera: 57200
Chen: 45100
Okafor: 62500
Sandoval: 43800`;

const Different = `THIS CHALLENGE IS NOT LIKE THE OTHERS.

Every debug challenge you have done had a defect
that made the program WRONG.

  a syntax error   it would not run
  a logic error    it ran and gave a wrong answer

This program has neither.

  It runs.
  Its arithmetic is correct.
  Its output is exactly what the code says.

And it should not be used.`;

const NotAFix = `THERE IS NO LINE TO CORRECT.

Do not look for one.

Your job is to find where the harm comes from,
say why, and then make a decision --
knowing that every option costs something.`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Debug Challenge: The Correct Program</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">
          No faults to fix &middot; on paper &middot; this one is different
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <Code code={Different} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Read This First" showLineNumbers={false} class="my-3" />

          <Code code={NotAFix} frame="code" lang="txt" title="And This" showLineNumbers={false} class="my-3" />

          <p class="text-body-secondary">
            <b>Paper only. Full sentences.</b>
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="program">
          <h2>The Program</h2>

          <p>
            A company uses this to work out what to offer a new hire. <b>All four
            candidates applied for the same role.</b>
          </p>

          <Code code={Program} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="offerFor" class="mb-4" />

          <h3>What It Prints</h3>

          <Code code={Output} frame="terminal" lang="txt" title="Correct Output" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-4" />
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>The Questions</h2>

          <h3>1. Confirm It Works</h3>
          <ol>
            <li><b>Work out all four offers by hand.</b> Do they match the output?</li>
            <li>Is there a syntax error? A logic error? Does the procedure do what its name says?</li>
            <li>Trace <code>offerFor(2)</code> line by line. Is every step correct?</li>
          </ol>

          <h3 class="mt-4">2. Find the Harm</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <b>Rivera and Chen have identical experience.</b> What is the difference in
              their offers?
            </li>
            <li>What was the difference in their <b>prior</b> salaries?</li>
            <li>
              <b>Compare those two numbers.</b> What has this program done to the gap it
              was given? <b>Say it as a percentage.</b>
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Which line causes this?</b> Quote it, and explain in two sentences why
              that line can produce a biased outcome despite containing no mistake.
            </li>
          </ol>

          <h3 class="mt-4">3. Which Kind of Bias</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>
              The exam names <b>two</b> sources of bias in computing innovations. Name
              both, and say which this is.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Describe what the other kind would look like in this same program.</b>
            </li>
            <li>
              Is this bias <b>intentional or unintentional</b>? Does your answer change
              whether it does harm?
            </li>
            <li>
              &quot;Biases can be embedded at all levels of software development.&quot;{" "}
              <b>Name three separate decisions</b> that went into this program, any of
              which could have introduced bias.
            </li>
          </ol>

          <h3 class="mt-4">4. Decide Something</h3>

          <p><b>Three options. None is free.</b></p>

          <table class="table table-sm align-middle mt-3">
            <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>What it fixes</th><th>What it costs or leaves unfixed</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><b>A.</b> Remove <code>priorSalary</code>. Offer a fixed band for the role, plus the experience bonus</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td><b>B.</b> Keep <code>priorSalary</code>, but publish that it is used</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td><b>C.</b> Keep it, and add a floor: no offer below 90% of the band midpoint</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <ol>
            <li><b>Which do you choose, and why?</b></li>
            <li><b>What does your choice still not fix?</b></li>
            <li>
              <b>Who should make this decision?</b> Not &quot;the programmer&quot; &mdash;
              name who, and why them.
            </li>
          </ol>

          <p class="mt-3">
            <b class="text-sn-theme">Question 1 has no correct answer. Question 2
            does.</b> Every option leaves something behind, and naming it is the whole
            skill.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            All four sections in full sentences, including your completed options table
            and your choice with its reasoning.
          </p>

          <p>Worth <b>4 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
